---
title: "The week I tracked one number"
description: "I drowned myself in dashboards until one metric made decisions easy."
date: "2026-07-24"
tags:
  - growth
  - founding
published: true
layout: docs
---

I used to check everything. Pipeline, impressions, stars, random Notion charts. End of the day I still didn't know if Algility was winning.

So I picked one number for the month: qualified calls booked. That's it. If a task didn't help that number, I parked it.

Weirdly, work got calmer. I wasn't "busy." I was either moving the number or I wasn't. Most weeks I only need that kind of honesty.
